course: dictionary
lesson: 15752
title: Trimmed: cut, decorate or average
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trimmed usually means cut a little, so that something looks neat or tidy. «Dad trimmed the hedge so the path was clear.» Dad cut away the messy edges, so the hedge looks neat.
explain: Trimmed can also mean made smaller by cutting away extra parts. «Mia trimmed her essay from six pages to four.» She cut out the words and parts she did not need. Trimmed is the past form of trim, so trim, trims and trimming belong to the same family.
explain: Trimmed can mean decorated along the edges. «The coat was trimmed with soft fur.» The fur is on the edges, not on the whole coat. Use the clues to choose the meaning: is the sentence about cutting, making smaller, or decorating?
explain: In maths, a trimmed mean is an average worked out after removing the highest and lowest values. The word has a special meaning there, so check the subject you are reading about.
fact: Trim means to cut a little, to make something neat.
fact: «Trimmed» is the past form of trim: «Sam trimmed his nails yesterday.»
fact: «Trimmed with» means decorated along the edges, as in «a dress trimmed with lace».
fact: A trimmed mean is an average made after removing the highest and lowest values.
fact: Phrases you will meet include «neatly trimmed», «trim the tree» and «trimmed down».
exercise: «Dad trimmed the hedge so the path was clear.» What does trimmed mean here? | *Cut a little to make it neat | Thrown away completely | Watered every day | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The coat was trimmed with soft fur.» What does trimmed mean here? | Made smaller | Washed and dried | *Decorated along the edges | Cut into small pieces
exercise: «Mia trimmed her essay from six pages to four.» What was taken away from the essay? | *Words and parts that were extra | The title | Pages were added to it | Her name and the date
test: In a trimmed mean, which values are removed before the average is worked out? | None at all | *The highest and lowest values | The middle values | The first two values
test: Which sentence uses trimmed to mean made smaller? | «The tree was trimmed with silver balls.» | «The garden was trimmed neatly on Sunday.» | *«Sam trimmed the extra pages from his story.» | «The dress was trimmed with lace.»
exam: What is a trimmed mean? | A mean that is always zero | *An average made after removing the highest and lowest values | Any mean that is very large | The first value in a list
